communications.communication:
To Whom It May Concern:

Pursuant to the California Public Records Act, I hereby request the following records:

Emails from March 1, 2026 through August 10, 2026 between your agency and any of the below email domains:

@anomalysix.com 
@penlink.com 
@cobwebs.com 
@creativeradicals.com 
@twosixtech.com 
@venntel.com 
@gravyanalytics.com 
@verint.com 

Please also include any emails (regardless of domain) that include any of the following keywords in the subject or body:

1) "Anomaly Six" or "Anomaly 6" or "Anomoly6"
2) "PenLink" or "Webloc" 
3) "Creative Radicals"
4) "Two Six Technologies"
5) "Venntel" or "Gravy Analytics"
6) "Unacast" 

Details: Please include any email attachments, intact URLs, and embedded photos in any responsive documents. I prefer original .eml or .ms or .mbox files that maintain the state of the original email. If multiple people received the same email from these vendors please feel free to de-duplicate (I only need 1 of each email) if it saves space and time.

The requested documents will be made available to the general public, and this request is not being made for commercial purposes.

In the event that there are fees, I would be grateful if you would inform me of the total charges in advance of fulfilling my request. I would prefer the request filled electronically, by e-mail attachment if available or CD-ROM if not.

Thank you in advance for your anticipated cooperation in this matter. I look forward to receiving your response to this request within 10 calendar days, as the statute requires.

Sincerely,

Shawn Segal
